 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "tQG5WqKaAAAJ",
   "from": "Frédéric Gosselin",
   "author": "bc11fbb928eb77ff",
   "date": "2017-11-22T17:54:43Z",
   "subject": "Problem with monitoring logProbs in some nimble versions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>this is to report a problem with some Nimble versions under Windows that were directly installed from Nimble website through calls such as:</div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#548dd4\">install.packages(&quot;nimble&quot;, repos = &quot;<a href=\"http://r-nimble.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r-nimble.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478905133000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0IvZ59-tgZMHFKBnb0PZ7U\">http://r-nimble.org</a>&quot;,\r\ntype = &quot;source&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\">we cannot monitor logProb variables.</font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\">For example,</font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"Courier New\" color=\"#9fc5e8\">ConfModel$addMonitors(&quot;logProb_Y1&quot;,&quot;logProb_Ycons1&quot;)</font><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Courier New\"><br></font></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Courier New\">gives me an error message after the </font></font><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Courier New\">buildMCMC command telling me that objects </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&quot;logProb_Y1&quot;,&quot;logProb_Ycons1&quot; do not exist.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">This problem does not seem to happen in other (older?) versions of Nimble.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Do you know where this comes from and if there is a solution for this?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Sincerely,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Frédéric</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">BTW: how can we know the version of Nimble? Is there a command line for this?</span></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mjc2SVzSAAAJ",
   "from": "David Pleydell",
   "author": "bebd85531a67ef86",
   "date": "2017-11-23T10:55:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: Problem with monitoring logProbs in some nimble versions",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">BTW: how can we know the version of Nimble? Is there a command line for this?</span></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Frederic</div><div><br></div><div>Regarding your final question, one option is to use help.start() and navigate to the index page of the Nimble package where the version number is displayed</div><div><br></div><div>However, a better (richer) alternative is to use the R command sessionInfo() - this provides a good summary of the versions of all the various package etc in your current R session.  </div><div><br></div><div>Best</div><div>David</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "IwW6nqfDAgAJ",
   "from": "ugoline godeau",
   "author": "4d992ac005b751e4",
   "date": "2017-11-29T09:40:51Z",
   "subject": "Re: Problem with monitoring logProbs in some nimble versions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div>Just for info, I just did the update to 0.6-8 and I still have the problem.</div><div>Last time I had to reinstall everything (Rtools, R and Nimble) and it worked but only for one week and then it&#39;s started to do the error again. </div><div>So I haven&#39;t done it again because I know it will not last.</div><div>Is there a solution ?</div><div>Thank you in advance for your answeres</div><div>Ugoline</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>Le mercredi 22 novembre 2017 18:54:43 UTC+1, Frédéric Gosselin a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>this is to report a problem with some Nimble versions under Windows that were directly installed from Nimble website through calls such as:</div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#548dd4\">install.packages(&quot;nimble&quot;, repos = &quot;<a href=\"http://r-nimble.org\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r-nimble.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478905136000&amp;usg=AOvVaw258PH9YKXaPcpD1DjBJ27Z\">http://r-nimble.org</a>&quot;,\r\ntype = &quot;source&quot;)</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\">we cannot monitor logProb variables.</font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\">For example,</font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><font face=\"Courier New\" color=\"#9fc5e8\">ConfModel$addMonitors(&quot;logProb_Y1&quot;,&quot;logProb_Ycons1&quot;)</font><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Courier New\"><br></font></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Courier New\">gives me an error message after the </font></font><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Courier New\">buildMCMC command telling me that objects </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">&quot;logProb_Y1&quot;,&quot;logProb_Ycons1&quot; do not exist.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">This problem does not seem to happen in other (older?) versions of Nimble.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Do you know where this comes from and if there is a solution for this?</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Sincerely,</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">Frédéric</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align:justify;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">BTW: how can we know the version of Nimble? Is there a command line for this?</span></p></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
